@model IdeaListView
@*
    The body of both tabs. They differ only in the heading and in the order the ideas
    arrive in, so the markup lives here once.

    Keeping one copy is not only tidiness. The end to end scenarios select by accessible
    structure and check both tabs, so two copies could drift apart and the same scenario
    would quietly be checking different things on each page.
*@
@if (Model.FoundNothing)
{
    @*
        A search that matched nothing is not an empty board, and the two must not share a
        sentence. The invitation to be the first person to propose an idea belongs only to
        the board that really has none.
    *@
    <div class="estado-vazio">
        <p>@UiText.NoSearchResults</p>
    </div>
}
else if (Model.Items.Count == 0)
{
    <div class="estado-vazio">
        <p>@UiText.EmptyList</p>
        <a class="botao botao-principal botao-grande" asp-page="/Nova">@UiText.SubmitIdeaButton</a>
    </div>
}
else
{
    @* The warning sits once above the list, and before every vote button in document
       order. Repeating it on each row would read it out dozens of times to somebody
       using a screen reader, for a rule that is the same for the whole page.

       A page that draws this partial more than once says both notes itself and turns
       these off, because they are about the page and not about one of its lists. *@
    @if (Model.ShowNotes)
    {
        <p class="aviso aviso-voto">@UiText.PublicVoteWarning</p>

        @*
            What the bar in each row is measured against. It sits outside the list rather
            than as its first item, because the end to end scenarios count the direct
            children of this ul and expect that number to be the number of ideas.
        *@
        <p class="legenda-apoio">@UiText.SupportBarLegend</p>
    }

    <ul class="lista-ideias">
        @foreach (IdeaListItem idea in Model.Items)
        {
            @*
                The row is a grid of two columns, and the wrapper below is what gives the
                left one something to be. The id and the vote form stay inside this same
                <li>: four end to end scenarios reach the button and the count through the
                id, so whatever happens inside here, this element goes on containing both.
            *@
            <li class="ideia" id="ideia-@idea.Id">
                <div class="ideia-corpo">
                    <h2 class="ideia-titulo" id="ideia-titulo-@idea.Id">
                        <a asp-page="/Detalhe" asp-route-id="@idea.Id">@idea.Title</a>
                    </h2>

                    <p class="ideia-meta">
                        <partial name="_Iniciais" model="@idea.AuthorDisplayName" />
                        <span class="ideia-autor">@idea.AuthorDisplayName</span>
                        <time datetime="@(idea.CreatedAt.ToString("s", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture))">@TimeZoneInfo.ConvertTimeFromUtc(idea.CreatedAt, displayTimeZone).ToString("d")</time>
                    </p>

                    @*
                        The last few people to vote, newest first. Nothing here is private
                        that was not already public: the warning above this list says a vote
                        is public, and the complete list of voters has always been on the
                        idea's own page. What changed is where a few of those names appear.

                        An idea nobody has voted on carries none, and then nothing is drawn
                        rather than an empty label standing on its own.
                    *@
                    @*
                        Only ever filled on the personal page, and only for this person's
                        own ideas. Everywhere else it is zero and nothing is drawn.
                    *@
                    @if (idea.NewVoteCount > 0)
                    {
                        <p class="ideia-votos-novos">@UiText.FormatNewVotes(idea.NewVoteCount)</p>
                    }

                    @if (idea.RecentVoterNames.Count > 0)
                    {
                        <p class="ideia-ultimos-votos">
                            <span class="etiqueta">@UiText.RecentVotesLabel</span>
                            @foreach (string voterName in idea.RecentVoterNames)
                            {
                                <partial name="_Iniciais" model="@voterName" />
                            }
                        </p>
                    }
                </div>

                <partial name="_VoteButton"
                         model="@(new VoteButtonModel { IdeaId = idea.Id, HasVoted = idea.HasVoted, VoteCount = idea.VoteCount, SearchTerm = Model.SearchTerm })" />

                @*
                    "7 votos" and then "de 8 pessoas no quadro". The count keeps the
                    wording the specification fixes and this finishes the sentence, so the
                    number the votes are a share of is on the card rather than in a
                    percentage that hides it.

                    That denominator moves: it is the people who have opened the board,
                    and it grows. Written as a share, the day a colleague arrives every
                    number on the page falls at once with nobody unvoting, and it reads as
                    support lost. Written out, the cause sits beside the effect.

                    Nothing is said on a card with no votes. "Sem votos de 8 pessoas" is a
                    sentence about nobody, and the empty bar already says it.
                *@
                @if (idea.VoteCount > 0 && Model.ArrivedPeopleCount > 0)
                {
                    <p class="ideia-de-quantos">@UiText.FormatArrivedPeople(Model.ArrivedPeopleCount)</p>
                }

                @*
                    How much support this idea has against the one leading the same list,
                    said in shape rather than in figures. It sits beside the count it stands
                    for, and the rule between rows is the row's own border, not this.

                    IT GOES OUT OF DATE, AND NOTHING SHOWS IT.

                    Docs/02 fixes that with JavaScript on, a vote changes only the button
                    and the count. The bar is neither, so it keeps the width the server sent
                    until the next page load, and so does the position of this row. The two
                    agree with each other: both say what the board looked like when the page
                    arrived, while the count says what you just did.

                    The error is one vote measured against the leader, so 1/leader. Where
                    the idea already had votes, that is a bar a little shorter than it
                    should be and it still reads as a bar: with a leader at seven it is
                    fourteen points.

                    WHERE THE IDEA HAD NONE, IT IS NOT A SHORT BAR. The width stays at
                    nought beside a count that has stopped saying none, so the row says
                    nobody supported a thing that was just supported. On a board whose
                    leader also has one vote the bar should be full and is empty, which is
                    the whole range, not fourteen points of it.

                    To see it, with JavaScript on, vote on any row reading "Sem votos" and
                    look at the bar. It takes a page load to go away. This paragraph used to
                    claim the error could not be seen, which was measured at the top of a
                    mature list and written as though it held for the list.

                    Keeping the bar live instead is not the free repair it looks like. The
                    order of the rows would stay stale either way, so this row's bar would
                    run longer than the one above it while sitting below it. And the server
                    would have to send the percentage along with the count, which Docs/02
                    does not allow. That is a decision about the specification, and it is
                    open rather than settled.
                *@
                <div class="apoio" style="--apoio: @idea.SupportPercent%"></div>
            </li>
        }
    </ul>
}
